= a justification for confirmation holism =
====== short ====== 

====== related to ====== 

= main =
Say I want to define a predicate true of just the symbol sequences produced by a
arbitrary given turing machine.

In one sense it can be done - I can define it matching each of the steps in the
turing machine and be sure that P(xyz) if and only if TM_produces(xyz)

but in another sense I cant - you cant prove equivalence of two turing machines.

But of course the resolution is that you can't in general - there must be
alternative ways that cannot be shown to be identical. (but there are some you
can show to be identical)

you can for any specified TM produce the matching predicate, but you cannot in
general determine that a predicate is true of just the strings produced by a
given TM

this justifies confirmation holism because ???
if there were a criteria - say simplicity, which ordered TM (or predicates) and
